invariant: INV-22
file: handshake_record.c
catches: unit
reason: hsr_refuse_alert reads a record of the alert type of any length as
  one alert, so three bytes from the peer read as its fatal alert and go
  unanswered, where RFC 9846 section 5.1 makes such a record exactly one
  2-byte alert and a message that does not parse is decode_error.
  bin/unit requires decode_error for one byte and for three.

--- old
    if (n != 2) {
        *alert = ALERT_DECODE_ERROR;
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
--- new
    if (n < 2) {
        *alert = ALERT_DECODE_ERROR;
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
